<title>INDIA: India's IDBI signs $100 mln loan.</title>
<headline>India's IDBI signs $100 mln loan.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Industrial Development Bank of India (IDBI) said it signed a $100.0 million syndicated loan of two year maturity.</p>
<p>&quot;The loan has been negotiated for the purpose of refinancing $100 million floating rate note due 1999 and is the lowest spread over LIBOR achieved by an Indian entity for such maturity,&quot; IDBI said in a statement.</p>
<p>The loan facility was arranged by Fuji Bank Ltd, Singapore branch along with the Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
